---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="Accessibility commitment for geographyofcrime.com, including tutorials and course material.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap stack prose">
      <p class="label">Accessibility · Last updated October 2026</p>
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p class="lede">Everything here, including tutorials and course material, should be usable by everyone.</p>

      <h2>The standard</h2>
      <p>This site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA, the standard most universities and public agencies use.</p>

      <h2>What is in place</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every page works with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus outline and a "skip to content" link.</li>
        <li>Text and controls meet AA color contrast in both light and dark mode.</li>
        <li>Animations are turned off for anyone who sets "reduce motion" on their device.</li>
        <li>The crime map always states its key finding in text, so the point does not depend on seeing colors.</li>
        <li>Pages are checked automatically for common accessibility errors each time the site is updated.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>In progress</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Reviewed captions on every video, and full transcripts on podcast episode pages.</li>
        <li>Text descriptions and downloadable data for map views used in course material.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Report a problem</h2>
      <p>If something on this site is hard to use, email the address on the <a href="/about/">About</a> page with the page and the issue. I aim to fix reported problems promptly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
